                <pb facs="0301" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg193"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 9 in No. 10.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Gens.
                            Montiel, Zavala, and Zelaya.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sabana Grande</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-05-31T16:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">May 31,</hi>—4
                            o’clock p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I most sincerely thank you for the kind terms in which you are pleased to refer
                    to my Government and to my modest efforts to serve the best interests of the
                    people of Nicaragua. And I warmly congratulate the people of this Republic and
                    of the cause of good government everywhere on the patriotic and self-sacrificing
                    spirit displayed by yourselves.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis Baker.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
